592186157523 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186158316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157523 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186158317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157523 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157523 #edb/ref 1045 "Evaluating Definite Integrals Using Symmetry" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157523 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186158295 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157523 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157523 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "0c713b1b-8699-5cdf-acd5-178d556abfff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158295 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186158316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158295 #edb/ref 1061 41319 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158295 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "33e51af5-883a-5d53-a82e-9983b0aab23d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158295 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186158564 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158296 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186158297 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158296 #edb/ref 1061 41320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158296 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9dffa825-7698-5068-9cf9-029959145880" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158296 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186157396 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158297 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186158298 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158297 #edb/ref 1061 41323 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158297 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a69a25f0-35d2-5e6f-99dc-f9e17ed11afa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158297 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186158565 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158298 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186158299 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158298 #edb/ref 1061 41324 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158298 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3dd1c1c0-5948-50f9-802e-942f886fd7e6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158298 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186157397 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158299 #edb/ref 1061 41371 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158299 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3288d02d-a5b0-5d8a-8137-f96ae6e90b23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158299 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186157398 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158316 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186158317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158316 #edb/ref 1061 41640 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158316 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2b925bf3-52e2-5fd3-a231-2bd9005b1e1c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158316 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186158566 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158317 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186158296 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158317 #edb/ref 1061 41641 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158317 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "55d52e16-03f0-5165-836c-65302f301bf0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158317 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186158567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158564 #edb/ref 1064 "Recall that $f(x)$ is an **even function** if\n\n$$\nf(-x) = f(x).\n$$\n\nThe graph of an even function is always symmetric about the $y$-axis.\n\n![](images/fc/fc57d05c6bef23243df97979c0680054c6ec66b836a97871970ee055c60eab4a.png)\n\nAlso recall that $g(x)$ is an **odd function** if\n\n$$\ng(-x) = -g(x).\n$$\n\nThe graph of an odd function always has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. In other words, if we rotate the graph $180^\\circ$ about the origin, the resulting graph looks the same.\n\n![](images/d2/d21ae289b641f26e3b43dc7035e2ea02147d44dc490f0ab5e6e34381ea4c2db3.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158564 #edb/ref 1065 6806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158564 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e9042a5a-4bbc-5b00-aec4-0982199b1ab9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158564 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158565 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's consider the odd function $f(x)$ shown below.\n\n![](images/7c/7c179ee67a04113130e65e3ce4b8581c969724c380fbe903423d023427d573f8.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\int_{-a}^a f(x) \\, \\textrm dx = 0\n$$\n\nbecause the positive and negative areas cancel each other out.\n\nFurthermore, by the adjacent intervals rule, we can write\n\n$$\n\\int_{-a}^0 f(x)  \\, \\textrm dx + \\int_{0}^a f(x)  \\, \\textrm dx = 0,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n\\int_{-a}^0 f(x)  \\, \\textrm dx = - \\int_{0}^a f(x)  \\, \\textrm dx.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158565 #edb/ref 1065 6807 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158565 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "9707c582-25f4-5558-b5b5-e6af4f83c071" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158565 #edb/ref 1067 "Integrals of Odd Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158566 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's consider our even function $f(x)$ once more.\n\n![](images/7a/7a1b83234d7d028484eb939146db822a087ebffa063ff74dcd3b73478acd0399.png)\n\nWhen we have a definite integral of an even function, we can often use symmetry to simplify it. \n\nFrom the picture above, we have that\n\n$$\n\\int_{-a}^0 f(x) \\, \\textrm dx = \\int_{0}^a f(x) \\, \\textrm dx = A.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =A+A \\\\  & =2A \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo summarize, if $f(x)$ is even, then\n\n$$\n\\int_{-a}^a f(x) \\, \\textrm dx  = 2\\int_{0}^a f(x) \\, \\textrm dx .\n$$\n\nThis rule is helpful because definite integrals where one of the integration limits is zero are often easier to evaluate." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158566 #edb/ref 1065 6850 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158566 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "340dd64d-312a-5516-b425-9cf0b512e446" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158566 #edb/ref 1067 "Integrals of Even Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158567 #edb/ref 1064 "Throughout this lesson, it's worth remembering that the basic trigonometric functions can be classified as even or odd. \n\n- $\\cos x$ is an even function:\n\n$$\n\\cos(-x) = \\cos x\n$$\n\nThis function is symmetric about the $y$-axis.\n\n![](images/68/684c18a8cbd2aa9cf478ff5a569add34a7157eea2fed7075a56a2cee2aec985f.png)\n\n- $\\sin x$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\sin(-x) = -\\sin x\n$$\n\nThis function has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin.\n\n![](images/91/911c92dd5f3d6924226b49f2f25aeba67c8dca676612ccf2830e3a15871a49d6.png)\n\n- $\\tan x$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\tan(-x) = -\\tan x\n$$\n\nThis function has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin.\n\n![](images/92/92e670859be89f70e0c8199a7b368e187ab30fd3682478832690ee842595b62f.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158567 #edb/ref 1065 6851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158567 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "6163a166-7434-5d31-846e-676e81407a7d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158567 #edb/ref 1067 "Trigonometric Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272893 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{A}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272893 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272893 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3a4bbb7d-18d6-5b61-997d-b85518d9f085" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186273680 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{1}{2}A" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186273680 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186273680 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "947e1701-dda4-539d-abc1-fe98fe7dc964" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186273752 #edb/ref 1080 "A" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186273752 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186273752 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9e50ecf2-3ff8-5c23-8e90-43e354e46ca2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274279 #edb/ref 1080 "-A" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274279 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274279 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d85bad73-fa5d-5455-afb4-82cf9a4293cf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274636 #edb/ref 1080 "2A" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274636 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274636 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fff717bf-fcc8-5e40-9aff-2c2401a6f86d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275037 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186272893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275037 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186273680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275037 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186273752 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275037 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186274279 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275037 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186274636 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275037 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275037 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275037 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186274279 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275037 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e5db26d1-9e5a-5da7-a51d-01407ba0e210" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275341 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186275037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275341 #edb/ref 1069 "q-156188" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275341 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275341 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that ${\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{x}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}\\,\\text{d}x=A,$ what is the value of ${\\int }_{-5}^{0}\\frac{x}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}\\,\\text{d}x?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275341 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c649e814-a4ed-51c9-ad8d-f8d4317c4c2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275341 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)=\\frac{x}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}$ is an odd function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =\\frac{(-x)}{{e}^{(-x)}+{e}^{-(-x)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-x)}{{e}^{-x}+{e}^{x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{x}{{e}^{-x}+{e}^{x}} \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)=\\frac{x}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}$ is an odd function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-5}^{5}\\frac{x}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, using the adjacent intervals rule for integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5}^{5}\\frac{x}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-5}^{0}\\frac{x}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\frac{x}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-5}^{0}\\frac{x}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}\\,\\text{d}x+A & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-5}^{0}\\frac{x}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413324 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186413345 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413324 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186413346 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413324 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186413347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413324 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186413348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413324 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186413349 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413324 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413324 #edb/ref 1045 "Evaluating Definite Integrals Using Symmetry" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413324 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186413348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413324 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413324 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413324 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "dd7f20dd-b98f-586f-b688-7ce1c3a853b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413325 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413325 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413325 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "130e6afa-dce0-5b08-819c-ef94704234fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413326 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413326 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413326 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "376dd84b-186c-5a4f-8a0a-85f3f4cc251e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413327 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413327 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413327 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "47aae119-de52-5a6f-b7a1-ed5cfb5a10e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413328 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 